<article class="env-lemma" id="01NT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01NT">Lemma <span data-tag="01NT">27.16.1</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/01NN" data-tag="01NN">27.15.1</a>. Let $d \geq 1$. Let $F_ d$ be the functor associated to $(S, \mathcal{A})$ above. Let $g : S' \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Set $\mathcal{A}' = g^*\mathcal{A}$. Let $F_ d'$ be the functor associated to $(S', \mathcal{A}')$ above. Then there is a canonical isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  F'_ d \cong h_{S'} \times _{h_ S} F_ d  \]
</div>
  <p> of functors. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      A quadruple $(d, f' : T \to S', \mathcal{L}', \psi ' : (f')^*(\mathcal{A}')^{(d)} \to \bigoplus _{n \geq 0} (\mathcal{L}')^{\otimes n})$ is the same as a quadruple $(d, f, \mathcal{L}, \psi : f^*\mathcal{A}^{(d)} \to \bigoplus _{n \geq 0} \mathcal{L}^{\otimes n})$ together with a factorization of $f$ as $f = g \circ f'$. Namely, the correspondence is $f = g \circ f'$, $\mathcal{L} = \mathcal{L}'$ and $\psi = \psi '$ via the identifications $(f')^*(\mathcal{A}')^{(d)} = (f')^*g^*(\mathcal{A}^{(d)}) = f^*\mathcal{A}^{(d)}$. Hence the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>